# Demo: test by trading (user standing order)

On MetaQuotes demo (`allow_live: false`) this chat **may open and close**
0.01-lot tickets whenever a measured test needs it. The user asked for this
until they say the bot is live-ready. That is **not** a profit promise and
not “the best bot ever” as a claim — it is permission to experiment.

## Every 20-minute `AGENT_LOOP_TICK` (and similar reviews)

1. Read heartbeat, risk halt, open tickets + floating PnL, last journal orders.
2. Name **one** hypothesis (spread-red, stack-into-loser, stale EMA vs live
   candle, margin 10019, etc.).
3. If a 0.01 open or a ticket close would test it, **do that trade** via the
   existing MT5 engine. Journal `event: probe` with why.
4. Do **not** flatten the whole book by default. Close extras / one symbol /
   one ticket when that is the test. Keep one clip if you are testing
   “stop averaging into red.”
5. Never `mt5.shutdown()`. Never `allow_live`. Never a second
   `run_broker_paper.py`. Unattended optimizer stays YAML-only (no orders).

```text
# ❌ BAD — 20-min tick only reports equity
# ✅ GOOD — “AUDCHF 4x red stack; close 3 extras, keep 1; enable no_stack_if_red”
```
